## Purpose

Freeze the exact corpus identity, case-set identity, and expected zero-tolerance
outcomes for the MFRP-P3 historical replay fixture before the first replay
invocation runs. This ledger is authored and frozen together with the fixture;
neither is edited after the first replay executes.

## Target / Source

Target: `governance/compat/fixtures/mfrp_p3_historical_replay.json`.

Source authority: `docs/work_orders/CVF_AGENT_WORK_ORDER_MFRP_P3_HISTORICAL_REPLAY_AND_FROZEN_DEFECT_LEDGER_2026-09-01.md`
and its paired baseline
`docs/baselines/CVF_GC018_MFRP_P3_HISTORICAL_REPLAY_AND_FROZEN_DEFECT_LEDGER_2026-09-01.md`.
The seven frozen historical sources are listed in the Source Verification
Block below with independently recomputed SHA-256 values.

## Scope / Methodology

1. Recompute all seven frozen historical source SHA-256 values and compare
   against the work order's Frozen Historical Source Set table.
2. Author the fixture corpus binding every case to one of the seven sources,
   labeling any synthetic mutation `SEEDED_DERIVATION` and every case sourced
   directly from a historical outcome `HISTORICAL_OUTCOME`.
3. Compute the corpus SHA-256 over the fixture file bytes exactly as written.
4. Compute the case-set digest as SHA-256 over the sorted UTF-8 case IDs
   joined by `LF` with one trailing `LF`.
5. Record both digests here with `freezeState: FROZEN_BEFORE_FIRST_REPLAY`
   before the first replay invocation runs.
6. Run the replay helper once; record first-run evidence in the worker return
   without editing this ledger or the fixture afterward.

