## Findings / Position

No findings are raised by this freeze record itself; it declares the
pre-replay expected state. Any replay divergence from this frozen expectation
is a false negative or false positive to be recorded in the worker return, not
in this ledger, since this ledger does not change after the first replay.

## Risk / Corrective Action

| Risk | Corrective action |
|---|---|
| corpus tuned after first replay to manufacture a pass | this ledger and the fixture are both frozen before first replay; the worker return records first-run evidence unedited |
| seeded mutation misrepresented as historical | every `SEEDED_DERIVATION` case is labeled honestly in the fixture and cross-referenced here; only `HISTORICAL_OUTCOME` cases claim a real historical result |
| zero-tolerance averaging | the reconciliation table above lists each class with an explicit non-zero case count; the replay helper reports per-class recall, never an aggregate |
| source hash silently refreshed | seven source hashes are pinned in `sourceManifest` and independently recomputed in the Source Verification Block above before this freeze |

## Decision / Disposition

`FROZEN_BEFORE_FIRST_REPLAY`. The fixture and this ledger are complete and
frozen. The next step is one replay invocation and preservation of its
first-run output in the worker return; this ledger itself receives no further
edits from this worker.

